USD: SEP_STR in a USD build without Python

usd_common.cc uses SEP_STR (BLI_path_util.h) without including it. The code is only compiled
when USD is built without Python support (#ifndef PXR_PYTHON_SUPPORT_ENABLED), which Blender's
own library builds never are, so the missing include went unnoticed. Haiku builds USD without
Python.

--- a/source/blender/io/usd/intern/usd_common.cc
+++ b/source/blender/io/usd/intern/usd_common.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 
 #include "BKE_appdir.h"
 
+#include "BLI_path_util.h"
+
 namespace blender::io::usd {
 
 void ensure_usd_plugin_path_registered()
